    },
    {
      "text": "If implementations become generatable, where does our value live? And our answer? Our value moves from implementation to specification.",
      "timestamp_sec": 60,
      "why": "frames the business consequence for infrastructure vendors"
    },
    {
      "text": "The product is no longer the implementation. The product is the specification, the protocol.",
      "timestamp_sec": 122,
      "why": "the sharpest statement of the strategic bet"
    },
    {
      "text": "The question is, can we repeatedly synthesize trusted servers from the same specification?",
      "timestamp_sec": 122,
      "why": "reframes the engineering problem from capability to repeatability and trust"
    },
    {
      "text": "The specification must be abstract. Only the implementation must be concrete.",
